    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "As an actress, Michelle Yeoh is often seen on the big screen. However, the "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Malaysian",
            "zh": "马来西亚人"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " always wants people to see her differently."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Yeoh "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "started out",
            "ref": "v-start-out"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in Hong Kong. That was forty years ago. Back then, "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "actresses",
            "ref": "v-actress"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " could usually only play young, helpless women. Most of the time, they were seen being protected by men—their “heroes”. Yeoh wanted something different. She wanted to be a “hero” and kick people in the face. The actress worked hard to learn "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "martial arts",
            "zh": "武术"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". She started to play alongside "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Jackie Chan",
            "zh": "成龙"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Jet Li",
            "zh": "李连杰"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". And people started to see her differently."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Yeoh quickly became famous in Asia. Soon, she began to get calls from Hollywood. The actress was excited. But when she got there, she "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "felt let down"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Most people in Hollywood were white. They cared little about people from other cultures. For an Asian actress, chances were rare."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But Yeoh tried to be seen differently. In 1997, she starred in the James Bond movie "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Tomorrow Never Dies"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". People saw a very different “"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Bond Girl",
            "zh": "邦女郎"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "”. Instead of waiting to be saved, Yeoh’s character saved 007’s life. She could do the same thing as the man."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Few believed someone from Asia could win the Oscar for Best Actress. On March 13, 2023, however, Yeoh did just that. She made history for her performance in "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Everything Everywhere All at Once"
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "",
            "zh": "《瞬息全宇宙》"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". People around the world now see Yeoh differently. And because of her, they see Asian actors and actresses differently."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Most teenagers today like young actors and actresses. They are "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "unlikely",
            "ref": "v-unlikely"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "idolise",
            "zh": "崇拜"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Yeoh (she’s in her sixties). But now that you’ve found out more about her, do you see her differently?"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
